			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T10:49:57.987Z",
			"content": "<p>Love this! And it looks like it would make 3rd party components more immediately compatible with my little definer.js script if I changed it to add `.js?nodefine&amp;define=false` (so it works with both your and <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:vrrdgcidwpvn4omvn7uuufoo\">@jakelazaroff.com</a>’s patterns) instead of just adding the .js extension</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:prsjlcqmyr3unqje5g6gzbxw/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7kweaz6c2e",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:prsjlcqmyr3unqje5g6gzbxw/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7kahk3xs2e",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/engelman.nl/post/3li7kweaz6c2e",
			"author": {
				"name": "Danny Engelman 🌷🏍️🛥️",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/engelman.nl",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:prsjlcqmyr3unqje5g6gzbxw/bafkreicmgiut2fprnqwxl77xndpf3jcrftazwaurgpy7lqotoz7b46qjne"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T11:02:03.941Z",
			"content": "<p>I extended Josh Wardle his Wordle (written with Web Components)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://dev.to/dannyengelman/more-wordle-mordle-extending-josh-his-web-components-4li\">dev.to/dannyengelma...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7ptqm3wc2b",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stuffbreaker.bsky.social/post/3li7ptqm3wc2b",
			"author": {
				"name": "Burton Smith",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stuffbreaker.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/bafkreiflfqfme6bk7akho6uhsi3bnjxrwgoh3gkb6lisi7lg4vhxjqaxzy"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T12:30:04.932Z",
			"content": "<p>I like the idea of self-contained definers, especially if you have custom logic for defining components.</p>\n<p>Because of the side-effect that comes with defining components in the same module as where the logic is, I've been a big proponent of splitting them into separate modules.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7ptqwprc2b",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7ptqm3wc2b",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stuffbreaker.bsky.social/post/3li7ptqwprc2b",
			"author": {
				"name": "Burton Smith",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stuffbreaker.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/bafkreiflfqfme6bk7akho6uhsi3bnjxrwgoh3gkb6lisi7lg4vhxjqaxzy"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T12:30:04.933Z",
			"content": "<p>That way you can import the module as-is from the definer from one module or you can import the class from another module if you want to customize the tag or extend the class.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:7jiqgk4co5kchm6gwgqhoc3c/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7vtho7k22f",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/coryrylan.com/post/3li7vtho7k22f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Cory Rylan",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/coryrylan.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:7jiqgk4co5kchm6gwgqhoc3c/bafkreifi6ijidsplgcj2b2ofddhottv4o2louvh2wircwwds4dqxqr4urq"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T14:17:18.012Z",
			"content": "<p>The way I've handled this is by making a secondary/separate import that auto defines the custom element.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/coryrylan/reusable-ui-component-api-guide?tab=readme-ov-file#side-effects\">github.com/coryrylan/re...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:24la36c5vk45r2sc4xscsikr/app.bsky.feed.post/3lia3yj5j4c2x",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/voxpelli.com/post/3lia3yj5j4c2x",
			"author": {
				"name": "Pelle Wessman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/voxpelli.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:24la36c5vk45r2sc4xscsikr/bafkreicdkr7cmuzc7kxnnvjz5bpe5ws3wgbnr5jiczzih6dqeoeu6uncgq"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-15T16:07:29.788Z",
			"content": "<p>Such a lovely blast from the past!</p>\n<p>It hadn’t crossed my mind that the ”import.meta.url” could be a replacement for the old way of finding the data by checking the DOM for script tags (and when synchronously loading a script, grabbing the last available element in the DOM or whatever it was)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lii7qpsbw22j",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:prsjlcqmyr3unqje5g6gzbxw/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7kweaz6c2e",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lii7qpsbw22j",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-18T21:36:01.200Z",
			"content": "<p>This thread has me thinking, thanks! <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/is-land/issues/32\">github.com/11ty/is-land...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3liia3vaw2c23",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:hewhabm3uw73cbz27uwuydcg/app.bsky.feed.post/3li6qsbqg7s24",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3liia3vaw2c23",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-18T21:42:16.022Z",
			"content": "<p>Mostly this was an artifact from &lt;is-land&gt; (which I’ve been working on) which has some static APIs it exposes around fallback content and initialization extensions — wanted those to be available globally. I don’t think I’d go so far as to say it makes sense everywhere!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3liia63uqis23",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:komsc4cibngambanqjhpwweu/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7kapwpoc2i",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3liia63uqis23",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-18T21:43:30.072Z",
			"content": "<p>Interesting! You may be interested in this discussion too: <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/is-land/issues/31\">github.com/11ty/is-land...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3liiaaya7p223",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:pefubtxqc5svtvsds725qgx3/app.bsky.feed.post/3li7ptqwprc2b",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3liiaaya7p223",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-18T21:45:06.917Z",
			"content": "<p>it feels a little heavy for one-off components for me but I can see the allure for larger systems!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
